<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1547">1547</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt was Land's Advocate of Holland from 1586 and the leading statesman of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. He organised its finances and government, helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1602 and negotiated the Twelve Years' Truce with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1609. Drawn into the religious conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/remonstrants">Remonstrants</a> and Counter-Remonstrants, he clashed with Stadtholder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-prince-of-orange">Maurice of Nassau</a>, was tried for treason and was beheaded in 1619.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johan-van-oldenbarnevelt.jpg" alt="Johan van Oldenbarnevelt" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johan_van_Oldenbarnevelt_(1547-1619),_by_workshop_of_Michiel_Jansz_van_Mierevelt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
